    {
      "id": "hvY-diwEg5alg4eIdkPOl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3484.1329408884008,
      "y": -2823.922142099765,
      "width": 912.299072265625,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "XzIAZv_33M04jHDZjnu_P"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 857874686,
      "version": 3947,
      "versionNonce": 1465876990,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763370835679,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Large language models sometimes guess when uncertain, producing plausible yet incorrect \nstatements instead of admitting uncertainty. Hallucinations persist due to the way most \nevaluations are graded—language models are optimized to be good test-takers, and guessing \nwhen uncertain improves test performance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMitigation #1 - Finetune\n=> Use model interrogation to discover model's knowledge, and fine tune on a new training \ndataset with knowledge-based refusals in cases where the model doesn't know, i.e. train \nthe model to reconize when it doesn't know\n\nMitigation #2 - Tools & RAG\n=> LLMs do not respond to user queries until they refer to a specified set of documents.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Large language models sometimes guess when uncertain, producing plausible yet incorrect \nstatements instead of admitting uncertainty. Hallucinations persist due to the way most \nevaluations are graded—language models are optimized to be good test-takers, and guessing \nwhen uncertain improves test performance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMitigation #1 - Finetune\n=> Use model interrogation to discover model's knowledge, and fine tune on a new training \ndataset with knowledge-based refusals in cases where the model doesn't know, i.e. train \nthe model to reconize when it doesn't know\n\nMitigation #2 - Tools & RAG\n=> LLMs do not respond to user queries until they refer to a specified set of documents.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ChCSJHi8UO5kAwkYoXd_z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -110.29498922257278,
      "y": -2803.0779773848394,
      "width": 912.5191650390625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 452041812,
      "version": 2545,
      "versionNonce": 1314553982,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763372972415,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Fine-tuning is cheaper then pre-training but still very complex!\nFirst test the different LLMs in context cabalities! --> play with system prompt\nWhen everything doesn't work fine tuning is a viable option (or the task is not well definable \nin natural language)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSome fine-tune options:\n1. Improve answer structure and format:\n    - tool calling.\n    - provide a certain answer style or format more consistently.\n2. Improve model capabilities on domain specific reasoning patterns.\n3. Improve answer robustness to noise and adherence to system prompt.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Fine-tuning is cheaper then pre-training but still very complex!\nFirst test the different LLMs in context cabalities! --> play with system prompt\nWhen everything doesn't work fine tuning is a viable option (or the task is not well definable \nin natural language)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSome fine-tune options:\n1. Improve answer structure and format:\n    - tool calling.\n    - provide a certain answer style or format more consistently.\n2. Improve model capabilities on domain specific reasoning patterns.\n3. Improve answer robustness to noise and adherence to system prompt.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uksK9v0Z7qiUf7VstlVys",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2004.5818918290638,
      "y": -1075.203725814815,
      "width": 1113.9189453125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 446109524,
      "version": 1692,
      "versionNonce": 662638498,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763985068340,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "LoRA freezes the pretrained model weights and injects trainable rank decomposition matrices into each\nlayer of the Transformer architecture, greatly reducing the number of trainable parameters for downstream tasks.\nA matrix decomposition is a factorization of a matrix into a product of matrices",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "LoRA freezes the pretrained model weights and injects trainable rank decomposition matrices into each\nlayer of the Transformer architecture, greatly reducing the number of trainable parameters for downstream tasks.\nA matrix decomposition is a factorization of a matrix into a product of matrices",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
