      "updated": 1763386193149,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Finetuned models in production",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Finetuned models in production",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4_aKLiw_UM0mv2dNghN01",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3497.4870813089415,
      "y": -1036.0886332364325,
      "width": 1002.3990478515625,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 647853140,
      "version": 2703,
      "versionNonce": 1110381520,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763386193149,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scenario Overview: you have several 7B fine-tuned language models, each tailored to a different \nclient or task. You want to serve all of them from a single GPU, dynamically loading the correct \nmodel when a client request arrives.\n\nThe router receives a client request -> decides which fine-tuned model to serve.\n\nProblem: Each fine-tuned model occupies ~30 GB in FP32.\n    ==> you can’t keep all of them resident in limited GPU memory.\n    ==> you must unload the current model and load the requested one from CPU RAM or disk\n\nLoading/unloading whole checkpoints trashes latency. Moving tens of gigabytes from \ndisk --> CPU --> GPU takes several seconds and during this time your application is idle. If requests \nalternate between different models, every swap causes a latency spike and overall throughput collapse.\n\nMoreover, once a model is loaded, the first request triggers additional setup due to cold-load latency.\n\nLoRA solve this with adapters.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Scenario Overview: you have several 7B fine-tuned language models, each tailored to a different \nclient or task. You want to serve all of them from a single GPU, dynamically loading the correct \nmodel when a client request arrives.\n\nThe router receives a client request -> decides which fine-tuned model to serve.\n\nProblem: Each fine-tuned model occupies ~30 GB in FP32.\n    ==> you can’t keep all of them resident in limited GPU memory.\n    ==> you must unload the current model and load the requested one from CPU RAM or disk\n\nLoading/unloading whole checkpoints trashes latency. Moving tens of gigabytes from \ndisk --> CPU --> GPU takes several seconds and during this time your application is idle. If requests \nalternate between different models, every swap causes a latency spike and overall throughput collapse.\n\nMoreover, once a model is loaded, the first request triggers additional setup due to cold-load latency.\n\nLoRA solve this with adapters.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ez0raD2uMxzL0gvixaK64",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -113.98261330181742,
      "y": -2250.0502612590813,
      "width": 805.6166538900814,
      "height": 49.428571428570685,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "eCGRHmuyBayyXhQyGB2zf",
        "EfLv7hh3D56F-yKHPl97D"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0YV",
