      "updated": 1763373044168,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Guidelines for Finetuning",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Guidelines for Finetuning",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nvjwv0zo48xjAsp4_oBmq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -108.25427401895547,
      "y": -2202.512044259483,
      "width": 972.69921875,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EfLv7hh3D56F-yKHPl97D"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1121016812,
      "version": 3205,
      "versionNonce": 2135274143,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764016477438,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Evaluate the hardware at your desposal based on the budget allocated on the project\n2. Pick a model size suitable to your hardware\n\n\n    Where:\n    - M: GPU memory (VRAM) expressed in gigabytes.\n    - P: The number of parameters in the model (e.g., 70 for a 70B model).\n    - Q: The number of bits used for loading the model (4 bytes/parameter in full-precision (FP32), \n        2 bytes/parameter in half-precision (BF16, FP16), 1 byte/parameter for 8-bit data types \n        (INT8, FP8), etc.)\n\n    A 7B model in full precision requires at least ~30GB. \n\n3. Do you want to train from scratch or refine a pre-trained method? In the case of LLM\n    (but not only), training from scartch is not a recommended option.\n4. Spend 70% of your time on data preparation. There is a reason why AI companies do not \n    release their data.\n5. create a train, eval and test split for tuning the model parameter, run the fitted model on \n    unseen data and provide an unbiased evaluation of a final model fit on the training data set.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Evaluate the hardware at your desposal based on the budget allocated on the project\n2. Pick a model size suitable to your hardware\n\n\n    Where:\n    - M: GPU memory (VRAM) expressed in gigabytes.\n    - P: The number of parameters in the model (e.g., 70 for a 70B model).\n    - Q: The number of bits used for loading the model (4 bytes/parameter in full-precision (FP32), \n        2 bytes/parameter in half-precision (BF16, FP16), 1 byte/parameter for 8-bit data types \n        (INT8, FP8), etc.)\n\n    A 7B model in full precision requires at least ~30GB. \n\n3. Do you want to train from scratch or refine a pre-trained method? In the case of LLM\n    (but not only), training from scartch is not a recommended option.\n4. Spend 70% of your time on data preparation. There is a reason why AI companies do not \n    release their data.\n5. create a train, eval and test split for tuning the model parameter, run the fitted model on \n    unseen data and provide an unbiased evaluation of a final model fit on the training data set.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0EZZ9hZjbchX9jwkQUN4M",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 304.89714970023454,
      "y": -2132.9898915177323,
      "width": 170.91187438964957,
      "height": 35.000000000000234,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EfLv7hh3D56F-yKHPl97D"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1061742188,
      "version": 856,
      "versionNonce": 459715774,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763373044168,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "M = P * Q/8",
      "fontSize": 28.000000000000185,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "M = P * Q/8",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NOzo_xsWhMQgIfYkQVwJd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2514.159264809906,
      "y": -2861.3474915084375,
      "width": 770.6166538900814,
      "height": 49.428571428570685,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "j5KVQCvXqCZ4sruozE3eu"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 151926228,
      "version": 4106,
      "versionNonce": 1234774178,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763369842685,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RAG hallucinations",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RAG hallucinations",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "v2UcNOiP44defuUcNEBbs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2511.1890319403856,
      "y": -2801.418920079867,
      "width": 973.0990600585938,
      "height": 1175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 452841324,
      "version": 3729,
      "versionNonce": 1658131838,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763372463529,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RAG retrieves facts from an external knowledge base in the attempt to:\n    1. helps pre-trained large language models generate up-to-date or OOD information and,\n    2. reduce hallucinations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRAG reduces LLM hallucinations by directly feeding the model with the information it needs to \ntalk about, instead of relying on its potentially outdated or messy internal knowledge.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRAG only mitigate hallucinations! A Stanford's study evaluated AI-driven legal research \ntools offered by LexisNexis (Lexis+ AI) and Thomson Reuters (Westlaw AI-Assisted Research and \nAsk Practical Law AI), and, for comparison, GPT-4.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nResult: while RAG appears to improve the performance of language models in answering legal\nqueries, the hallucination problem persists at significant levels. AI research tools made by\nLexisNexis (Lexis+ AI) and Thomson Reuters (Westlaw AI-Assisted Research and\nAsk Practical Law AI) each hallucinate between 17% and 33% of the time. \n\nA response is considered hallucinated if it is either incorrect or misgrounded. In other words, if a \nmodel answer contains any factually inaccurate information or if key factual propositions are cited \nbut the model misinterprets the source or reference an inapplicable source. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RAG retrieves facts from an external knowledge base in the attempt to:\n    1. helps pre-trained large language models generate up-to-date or OOD information and,\n    2. reduce hallucinations.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRAG reduces LLM hallucinations by directly feeding the model with the information it needs to \ntalk about, instead of relying on its potentially outdated or messy internal knowledge.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRAG only mitigate hallucinations! A Stanford's study evaluated AI-driven legal research \ntools offered by LexisNexis (Lexis+ AI) and Thomson Reuters (Westlaw AI-Assisted Research and \nAsk Practical Law AI), and, for comparison, GPT-4.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nResult: while RAG appears to improve the performance of language models in answering legal\nqueries, the hallucination problem persists at significant levels. AI research tools made by\nLexisNexis (Lexis+ AI) and Thomson Reuters (Westlaw AI-Assisted Research and\nAsk Practical Law AI) each hallucinate between 17% and 33% of the time. \n\nA response is considered hallucinated if it is either incorrect or misgrounded. In other words, if a \nmodel answer contains any factually inaccurate information or if key factual propositions are cited \nbut the model misinterprets the source or reference an inapplicable source. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
