      "updated": 1763369901489,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why does RAG hallucinate?",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why does RAG hallucinate?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kB-zqBNxFlndBdoGtDd0J",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1228.5703286685643,
      "y": -2820.3018726085756,
      "width": 950.939208984375,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "Krtq6Xj_OC-0AhpIS8XmJ"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1511477329,
      "version": 3917,
      "versionNonce": 106589374,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763372337953,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Fusion Problems: The generator might \"fuse\" information across documents in misleading ways. \n    Even if the documents are accurate, the model might synthesize incorrect conclusions.\n2. Retrieval Issues: The retriever may fetch documents that are topically relevant but factually \n    off, or even misleading. If the retriever isn't well-tuned, this noise propagates.\n\n\nWe will use fine-tuning to make the model more resistent to noise. In other words improve its\nability to evaluate the relevancy of the retrieved context with respect to the user query.\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Fusion Problems: The generator might \"fuse\" information across documents in misleading ways. \n    Even if the documents are accurate, the model might synthesize incorrect conclusions.\n2. Retrieval Issues: The retriever may fetch documents that are topically relevant but factually \n    off, or even misleading. If the retriever isn't well-tuned, this noise propagates.\n\n\nWe will use fine-tuning to make the model more resistent to noise. In other words improve its\nability to evaluate the relevancy of the retrieved context with respect to the user query.\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
