      "updated": 1763370840432,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Vague recollection vs. Working memory",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Vague recollection vs. Working memory",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YIm2MPZCsgKt6jQ8npWx-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3483.0038000401973,
      "y": -2020.1576005570455,
      "width": 944.0789794921875,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "PlJWiBk1JG4LixPOfGp5H",
        "RYdhxYt7-CHZRki7W5tgL",
        "cnh75oBXfOLigsi_CzMQu"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 642210494,
      "version": 4068,
      "versionNonce": 799542654,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763371567599,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Knowledge in the parameters --> Vague recollection (e.g. of something you read 1 month ago)\nKnowledge in the tokens of the context window --> Working memory\n\nDue to self-attention, the model attended to components of the context close to the question",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Knowledge in the parameters --> Vague recollection (e.g. of something you read 1 month ago)\nKnowledge in the tokens of the context window --> Working memory\n\nDue to self-attention, the model attended to components of the context close to the question",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2gfdVwVCmjs7_oOed8fxF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1225.2988266219909,
      "y": -2586.714448872068,
      "width": 805.6166538900814,
      "height": 49.428571428570685,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "O6INNbKMcdOKL9MO1TvEt"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1107812588,
      "version": 3931,
      "versionNonce": 1886308478,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763372690320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Fine-tuning for hallucination mitigation",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Fine-tuning for hallucination mitigation",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "k5TLp-dPc5X_EIQIbJa-z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1220.9193031208567,
      "y": -2517.2590774695072,
      "width": 1013.2391357421875,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2137434196,
      "version": 3681,
      "versionNonce": 689866338,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763372690320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why not just fine-tune on a small factual dataset to update the LLM's internal knowledge and simplify \nthe whole system.\n\nUnfortunately, fine-tuning does not work for knowledge update.\nIt was studied the impact of such exposure to new knowledge on the capability of\nthe fine-tuned model to utilize its pre-existing knowledge. \n    1. LLMs struggle to acquire new factual knowledge through fine-tuning. New knowledge \n        introduced by fine-tuning are learned significantly slower than those consistent with the \n        model’s knowledge.\n    2. examples with new knowledge are eventually learned, they linearly increase the model’s \n        tendency to hallucinate.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe will follow Meta's principle that post-training should align the model to “know what it knows” rather \nthan add knowledge. Rather then giving them model new capabilities, fine-tuning in the context of \nhallucinations is used to correct a bahaviour.\n\nSo RAG stays and we correct the behaviour of the LLM to give more relevant answers.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why not just fine-tune on a small factual dataset to update the LLM's internal knowledge and simplify \nthe whole system.\n\nUnfortunately, fine-tuning does not work for knowledge update.\nIt was studied the impact of such exposure to new knowledge on the capability of\nthe fine-tuned model to utilize its pre-existing knowledge. \n    1. LLMs struggle to acquire new factual knowledge through fine-tuning. New knowledge \n        introduced by fine-tuning are learned significantly slower than those consistent with the \n        model’s knowledge.\n    2. examples with new knowledge are eventually learned, they linearly increase the model’s \n        tendency to hallucinate.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe will follow Meta's principle that post-training should align the model to “know what it knows” rather \nthan add knowledge. Rather then giving them model new capabilities, fine-tuning in the context of \nhallucinations is used to correct a bahaviour.\n\nSo RAG stays and we correct the behaviour of the LLM to give more relevant answers.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
