    {
      "id": "KR-ZxAUCSadaqE8vgeFE9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3493.663648286986,
      "y": -466.57823740161507,
      "width": 983.2791137695312,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2012624098,
      "version": 3030,
      "versionNonce": 1136156624,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763386193149,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Pre-trained models have a very low intrinsic dimension\n    --> there exists a low dimension reparameterization that is as effective for fine-tuning as the \n        full parameter space. \n\nFor example, by optimizing only 200 trainable parameters, it was possible to tune a RoBERTa model \nto achieve 90% of the full parameter performance levels on MRPC.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis happens because large models have already learned a large numebr of feature needed for the \nspecific task at hand, therefore need minimum adaptation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Pre-trained models have a very low intrinsic dimension\n    --> there exists a low dimension reparameterization that is as effective for fine-tuning as the \n        full parameter space. \n\nFor example, by optimizing only 200 trainable parameters, it was possible to tune a RoBERTa model \nto achieve 90% of the full parameter performance levels on MRPC.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis happens because large models have already learned a large numebr of feature needed for the \nspecific task at hand, therefore need minimum adaptation.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
